          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em projective representation
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            up to a central term: a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PGL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\longrightarrow PGL(V)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+general+linear+group"} projective general linear group
            of some
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#GroupExtensionAndCocycle The group extension and its cocycle
          %p
            By construction, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  1 \to \mathbb{K}^\times \longrightarrow GL(V) \longrightarrow PGL(V)\to 1
          %p
            which exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PGL(V)
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}^\times
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Grp
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PGL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{Grp}(PGL(V),\mathbb{K}^\times)
          %p
            It is useful to re-express this equivalently in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            via the discussion at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping and delooping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon G\longrightarrow H
            are equivalently maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\phi \colon \mathbf{B}G\longrightarrow \mathbf{B}H
            between their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
          %p
            In terms of this the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extension"} group extension
            and its classifying cocycle is exhibited by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deloopings"} deloopings
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi PGL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi c
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ×
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}\mathbb{K}^*&amp; \longrightarrow &amp; \mathbf{B}GL(V) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;\longrightarrow&amp;\mathbf{B}PGL(V) &amp;\stackrel{c}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{K}^\times
                  }
                  \\,.
          %h3#RelationToGenuineRepresentations Relation to genuine representations
          %p
            Via the projection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PGL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)\to PGL(V)=GL(V)/\mathbb{K}^\times
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            induces a projective representation.
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            %a{:href => "#GroupExtensionAndCocycle"} above
            means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            to lift a given projective representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\rho \colon \mathbf{B}G\longrightarrow \mathbf{B} PGL(V)
            to a linear representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \rho
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mover
                                  %mi ρ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi PGL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi c
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;  &amp; \mathbf{B}GL(V) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\mathbf{B}\hat \rho}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}G &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{B}\rho}{\longrightarrow}&amp;\mathbf{B}PGL(V) &amp;\stackrel{c}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{K}^\times
                  }
          %p
            is the class of the 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∘
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(\rho)\coloneqq c \circ \mathbf{B}\rho
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
            class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Grp
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2_{Grp}(G,\mathbb{K}^\times)
          %h3#as_twisted_linear_representations As twisted linear representations
          %p
            By the
            %a{:href => "#GroupExtensionAndCocycle"} above
            and the discussion at
            %em
              %a{:href => "group+extension#FormulationInHomotopyTheory"} group extension – Central group extensions – Formulation in homotopy theory
            the cocycle map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}c \colon \mathbf{B}PGL(V)\to \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{K}^\times
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            may be represented by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zigzag"} zigzag
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-anafunctor"}> 2-anafunctor
            ”) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complexes"} crossed complexes
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ×
                          %mo →
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝕂
                            %mo ×
                          %mo →
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mo ≃
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi PGL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{B}(\mathbb{K}^\times \to GL(V)) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \mathbf{B}(\mathbb{K}^\times \to 1)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}PGL(V)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕂
                    %mo ×
                  %mo →
                  %mi GL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}(\mathbb{K}^\times \to GL(V))
            looks schematically like
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ⇓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{p_1}}\nearrow &amp;\Downarrow^{\mathrlap{k}}&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{p_2}}
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \underset{k p_1 p_2}{\longrightarrow}&amp;&amp; \ast
                  }
                  \\right\}
          %p
            This shows that a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi PGL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G\to \mathbf{B}PGL(V)
            may equivalently be represented by two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            (not group homomorphisms in general!)
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \colon G\to GL(V)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝕂
                        %mo ×
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \colon G\times G\to \mathbb{K}^\times
          %p
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ,
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g,h \in G
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho(g)\rho(h)=\lambda(g,h)\rho(g h)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group 2-cocycle
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                with values in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝕂
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{K}^*
                representing the above cohomology class of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mi ρ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_\rho
          %p This is the form in which projective representations are often discussed in the literature.
          %h3#as_genuine_representations_after_extensions As genuine representations after extensions
          %p
            Alternatively, one may consider the
            %a{:href => "#RelationToGenuineRepresentations"} above
            diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi GL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi ρ
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi PGL
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
